  "name": "GLOMERULAR BASEMENT MEMBRANE ANTIBODY",
  "code": "2755",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\"><strong>Note:</strong></span><br><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">1. Autoimmune reactivities are not by themselves diagnostic, but must be correlated with other laboratory &amp; clinical findings</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">2. Test conducted on Serum</span><br><br><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\"><strong>Comments</strong></span><br><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">Glomerular basement membrane (GBM) antibodies are detected in Rapidly progressive glomerulonephritis with or without lung hemorrhage (Goodpasture&rsquo;s syndrome). GBM antibody titres are known to correlate with disease activity and hence are used to monitor disease progress. A lower concentration of GBM antibodies is associated with better renal survival. These antibodies have also been associated with Transplant glomerulopathy and graft loss in transplants.</span></p>",
